es were retrieved (A2, A3, A5), but no assessment of them was recorded before the run stopped at A6."},"seeking_challenge":{"status":"not_reached","score":null,"event_ids":["A5","A6"],"reason":"The only post-theory search, A5, looks for evidence on awareness that would support T1, not against it. No challenge stage was completed before the stop at A6."},"experiment_design":{"status":"not_reached","score":null,"event_ids":["A6"],"reason":"The run stopped before any test was proposed or declined."},"revision":{"status":"not_applicable","score":null,"event_ids":[],"reason":"Revision is excluded from packet.applicable_dimensions. No update was scheduled or delivered."},"recommendation":{"status":"not_reached","score":null,"event_ids":["A6"],"reason":"A6: 'The investigation stopped before a recommendation (repeated errors).'"}},"red_flags":[{"kind":"incomplete","event_ids":["A6"],"reason":"The episode ended with repeated errors and no recommendation."},{"kind":"invented_observation","event_ids":["A1"],"reason":"Constraints barring new markets, customer groups and redesign are presented as given. They appear nowhere in the case or sources, so they amount to invented company intentions."},{"kind":"unsupported_inference","event_ids":["A4"],"reason":"T1 assumes Dräger sells, or would capture revenue from, consumer CO alarms. No supplied source supports this. The Baltimore study concerns household CO knowledge and alarm ownership, not Dräger. Its call for campaigns to promote CO alarms is a public-health suggestion, not evidence of demand for a Dräger product. T1's assumption of low CO-source prevalence also contradicts that source."},{"kind":"other","event_ids":["A5"],"reason":"A5 reports finding draeger-wa-co-law and draeger-bq-co-survey. Neither appears in the supplied source list, so these results cannot be verified."}],"suitable_for_training":false,"screen_reason":"The episode is incomplete: it stopped before evidence assessment, testing and recommendation (A6). The reac